package diskstore

// RequireQuorum is the write gate for a store declaring (spec.quorum_write):
// it refuses the write unless durableCopies reaches minDurableCopies.
//
// The generated per-store Require<Type>Quorum calls it with the store's
// declared floor; the store's write path calls that with the number of distinct
// nodes that will hold the value durably — only the store knows that number.
// Below the floor the write is REFUSED (FAILED_PRECONDITION) before any local
// effect. It is deliberately not a degrade-to-whatever-the-cluster-has: a
// production cluster that has lost members looks identical to a one-node
// development tree, so an implicit degrade removes the guarantee exactly where
// it was needed. A single node is a legal configuration, declared as
// min_durable_copies: 1.
//
// What counts as a "durable copy" is the store's own statement — for an
// in-memory replicated store it is the synchronous replica count, for a
// disk-backed one it is the number of logs the record has been fsync'd to. This
// gate compares the two numbers; it does not decide what they mean.
func RequireQuorum(store string, durableCopies, minDurableCopies int) error {
	if durableCopies < minDurableCopies {
		return ErrBelowQuorum(store, durableCopies, minDurableCopies)
	}
	return nil
}

// LocalRows is implemented by a service_store whose rows are PARTITIONED across
// a cluster, to narrow the roll baseline to the rows this node is responsible
// for.
//
// A redo log is single-writer, single-process, on the service's own volume —
// so in a clustered service each node owns a PARTIAL log, and recovery is the
// union of the reachable nodes' logs. The roll baseline has to keep that
// invariant: List(nil) returns the whole cluster's rows, so an unnarrowed
// baseline makes every node's log claim keys it does not own and never will
// again, and the union can no longer resolve staleness by ownership.
//
// A store that does not implement it keeps the whole-store baseline, which is
// correct for a single-process store.
type LocalRows interface {
	// IsLocalRow reports whether key is a row this node currently owns or
	// backs up, i.e. one that belongs in this node's roll baseline.
	IsLocalRow(key string) bool
}

// LocalRecords narrows records to the rows store reports as local when it
// implements LocalRows, and returns records unchanged otherwise.
func LocalRecords(store any, records []*Record) []*Record {
	local, ok := store.(LocalRows)
	if !ok {
		return records
	}
	scoped := make([]*Record, 0, len(records))
	for _, rec := range records {
		if local.IsLocalRow(rec.Key) {
			scoped = append(scoped, rec)
		}
	}
	return scoped
}
